Ainkrad for Mac: End User Licence Agreement

Version 1, 19 November 2026. Draft text for the public beta: have it reviewed before the announcement.

1. What this is. This agreement is between you and AinkradHQ ("Ainkrad") about the Ainkrad for Mac application and the updates
   Ainkrad delivers for it (the "App"). By installing or using the App you accept it. If you do not accept it, do not use the App.

2. Your licence. Ainkrad gives you a free, non-exclusive, non-transferable licence to install and use the App on Macs you own or
   control, for personal and commercial use. The App connects to a Core you run yourself; the Core has its own licence.

3. What you may not do. You may not copy or redistribute the App, sell, rent or sublicense it, remove or change its notices or
   signatures, or reverse engineer or decompile it, except where the law lets you do so despite this clause. Parts of the App come
   from open-source projects under their own licences, listed in the App's About screen; those licences apply to those parts.

4. Updates. The App updates itself. Each update is signed, and the App installs only updates signed with Ainkrad's key. An update
   is covered by this agreement unless it comes with a newer one.

5. Crash reports. The App can send a crash report to Ainkrad's own server: the app version, the macOS version, the CPU and where it
   stopped. It holds no names, files, Core addresses or anything you typed. It is on by default and you can turn it off in
   Settings, Privacy, or on the first screen.

6. Your data. The App keeps your work on your Core and your Mac. Ainkrad does not receive it. Accounts and keys you add belong to
   you and stay on your Core.

7. Third-party services. If you sign in to an AI provider with a subscription, you do so at your own risk and under that provider's
   terms. Ainkrad is not responsible for what a provider allows or charges.

8. No warranty. The App is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, including fitness for a purpose and non-infringement.

9. Limit of liability. To the extent the law allows, Ainkrad is not liable for indirect or consequential loss, lost data or lost
   profit, and its total liability is limited to what you paid for the App (nothing, while it is free).

10. Ending. This agreement ends if you break it. Then you stop using the App and delete it. Clauses 3, 8 and 9 stay in force.

11. Law. The law of the place where Ainkrad is established governs this agreement, and its courts decide disputes, unless a
    mandatory consumer law says otherwise.

